- If you use the simplified home‑office method instead: 130 sq ft × $5 = $650 (less than the regular calculation above)

Using the regular method (which gives the larger deduction here), total business deductions ≈ $1,350 + $4,328 = $5,678
- Net self‑employment profit ≈ $22,100 − $5,678 = $16,422

Step C — Self‑employment tax and deductible half
- Self‑employment tax is computed on 92.35% of net SE profit:
  - SE taxable earnings ≈ 16,422 × 0.9235 ≈ 15,173
  - SE tax ≈ 15,173 × 15.3% ≈ $2,323
  - Half of SE tax is an above‑the‑line deduction ≈ $1,161 (this reduces AGI)

Step D — Student loan interest adjustment
- The maximum student loan interest deduction allowed for 2023 is $2,500. You cannot deduct $4,800 in 2023; if $4,800 is interest accumulated across prior years, that cannot be carried forward as this deduction is only for interest paid in the tax year.
- The deduction phases out by MAGI for MFJ (2023 phaseout roughly $155,000–$185,000). With the numbers above (AGI before the deduction will be well under $155k), you are likely eligible for the full $2,500 — assuming you actually paid $2,500+ of student loan interest in 2023 and it is for a qualifying student loan.

