Step F — Itemize vs standard
- Known itemizable deduction (charity) = $1,350 (you can include charitable contribution only on Schedule A if you itemize).
- The standard deduction for 2023 MFJ = $27,700.
- Since $1,350 << $27,700, you’ll almost certainly take the standard deduction.
- Important: The home‑office and other business deductions are claimed on Schedule C (and lower AGI) regardless of whether you take the standard deduction — they are not part of Schedule A itemizing decision.

Other items you should consider
- 20% QBI (Qualified Business Income) deduction: you may be eligible for up to 20% of QBI from your Schedule C business (subject to limitations). Given your income and the small net business profit, you’re likely eligible for some QBI deduction — check Form 8995/Form 8995‑A rules (or ask a preparer).
