- State return: you’ll also file Illinois Form IL‑1040. Illinois has its own rules and flat tax; charitable contribution handling differs — check IL instructions or your preparer.

Forms you’ll most likely need
- Form 1040 (U.S. Individual Income Tax Return)
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — report the $22,100 and business expenses including home office allocation if using the regular method
- Schedule SE (Self‑Employment Tax) — to compute SE tax
