- The 22,100 looks like self‑employment income — report it on Schedule C, pay self‑employment (SE) tax on net profit (Schedule SE), and you can deduct ordinary business expenses (including home office) on Schedule C.
- Student loan interest is an “above‑the‑line” adjustment (not on Schedule A) and is limited (see details below).
