- Schedule A — only if you choose to itemize (likely you will NOT)
- Keep W‑2 (Riverside Hospital), 1099‑INTs, any 1099‑NEC/1099‑MISC you receive for the $22,100, and receipts for charitable contributions.
State (Illinois)
- IL Form IL‑1040 — Illinois taxes income; special rules vary (e.g., Illinois may not allow the student loan interest adjustment the same way). Check IL instructions or your tax pro for state specifics.

Other practical points
- Make sure you report the full self‑employment income even if you don’t receive 1099s.
- Keep receipts for the Habitat donation, home office allocation (floor plan / square footage calculations), and any business receipts for the $1,350 in unreimbursed expenses.
