1) What you can deduct (high level)
- Student loan interest: This is an “above-the-line” adjustment to income (not an itemized deduction). The maximum deduction for 2023 is $2,500 (even if you paid more). Eligibility is phased out for MAGI between $145,000 and $175,000 for MFJ; given the income numbers you provided, you appear to be under the phaseout range and would generally be eligible for the full $2,500 — but I need to confirm exactly what year(s) the $4,800 interest was paid.
