- Schedule SE (Self-Employment Tax) — to compute the self-employment tax (Social Security and Medicare) on your net self-employment earnings; half of that tax is an adjustment to income.
- Form 8995 (or 8995-A) — Qualified Business Income deduction (QBI) if you want to claim the 20% QBI deduction for your business income (you likely qualify for a simple 8995).
