  - SE tax ≈ 15.3% on 92.35% of net profit → roughly $2,300 (estimate above).  
- You can deduct half of your SE tax as an “above‑the‑line” adjustment to income (reported on Schedule 1).

4) Student loan interest
- The student loan interest deduction max is $2,500 per return for 2023 (not the full $4,800 you paid). The deduction is subject to income phaseouts (married filing jointly phaseouts start well above your likely AGI here), so with the AGI estimates below you should be able to take the full $2,500. You’ll need Form 1098‑E from Sallie Mae or other proof of interest paid.

5) Charitable contribution ($1,350)
