- Illinois: IL‑1040 (state return). Illinois tax is flat (4.95% for 2023) and uses federal AGI as a starting point; follow IL instructions for any state-specific adjustments.

Important treatment notes and tax mechanics
- Home office deduction is only allowed for self‑employment/business use (Schedule C). It must be regular and exclusive use and used as principal place of business.
- If you’re a renter, your rent is fully eligible for allocation for home office (no mortgage interest/form 1098 required).
