- Home office: deductible only if you are self-employed (or a partner / certain business owners). Two methods:
  - Simplified: $5 per square foot up to 300 sq ft → 130 sq ft × $5 = $650.
  - Regular: pro rata share of allowable home expenses. Based on your numbers: business % = 130 / 620 ≈ 20.97%. Rent $1,720/mo × 12 = $20,640 × 20.97% ≈ $4,330 (plus allocable utilities if you pay them and can document them). For a renter with the numbers you gave the regular method is likely larger than the simplified method.
  - Home-office deduction for self-employed is reported on Schedule C (or Form 8829 for the regular method). It cannot be taken if you are an employee (W-2) with unreimbursed expenses (unless very rare exceptions apply).
