4. Do you pay utilities or other housing costs you want to allocate to the home office (electricity, internet, renter’s insurance)? That increases the regular-method home-office deduction.
5. Do you have any state/local tax paid, mortgage interest, or other itemizable items you haven’t mentioned? (This could change the standard vs itemize conclusion.)

