- Self-employment income: $22,100
- Interest income: $1,210
- Business expenses (assume $1,350) → Schedule C net before home office = 22,100 - 1,350 = 20,750
- Home office (actual method rent share): annual rent $20,640 × 130/620 ≈ $4,330
- Net Schedule C profit after home office = 20,750 - 4,330 = 16,420
- Self-employment tax (approx): net earnings for SE tax = 0.9235 × 16,420 ≈ 15,171 → SE tax ≈ 15,171 × 15.3% ≈ $2,323
- Half of SE tax deductible (above-the-line): ≈ $1,161
- Taxable income before standard/itemized deduction roughly = wages + (Schedule C profit) + interest - above-the-line deductions:
  - 79,400 + 16,420 + 1,210 - 1,161 ≈ 95,869
  - Subtract MFJ standard deduction 27,700 → taxable income ≈ 68,169
