- Student loan 1098-E (if you paid interest in 2023); otherwise documentation of interest paid in 2023
- Any estimated tax payments or tax withholding information from your W-2

8) Other practical items
- Estimated taxes: As a self-employed earner you may owe quarterly estimated tax payments and self-employment tax — if you didn’t make estimates in 2023, check for underpayment penalty exposure.
- QBI: The 20% qualified-business-income deduction can reduce taxable income. It’s computed on Form 8995 (or 8995-A if thresholds apply). For your approximate net business profits these look favorable for a QBI deduction, but the exact amount depends on final taxable income and filing specifics.
- State taxes: Illinois has its own rules and flat rate (4.95% in 2023). Your state tax owed will depend on total income; work with IL instructions or a tax preparer to confirm.

