- Conclusion: Unless you have substantial mortgage interest, large property taxes, or other sizable deductible items you didn’t list, you’ll almost certainly be better off taking the standard deduction. The home-office deduction still benefits you because it reduces your Schedule C net income (it’s not part of Schedule A).

7) Self‑employment tax and related items
- Your self‑employment (SE) tax is computed on net earnings from self‑employment (Schedule SE); you pay both halves (15.3%) but can deduct one-half of SE tax on Schedule 1 as an adjustment to income.
