  - Estimated AGI ≈ $93,372
- Standard deduction (MFJ) = $27,700 → taxable income ≈ $65,672

Bottom line from the numbers above:
- You will almost certainly take the standard deduction (itemizing with only $1,350 charitable donations is far less than $27,700).
- The home-office deduction (if legitimately used exclusively and regularly for the business) and allowable business expenses reduce your self-employment net income and therefore both income tax and self-employment tax.
- You’ll owe self-employment tax on net self-employment income (but you get to deduct half of that on Form 1040).
- Student loan interest paid will likely be limited to $2,500 (subject to income phaseout) — you should confirm your MAGI for the exact phaseout.

