  - Self-employment tax base = 20,100 × 0.9235 = 18,568 → SE tax ≈ 18,568 × 0.153 ≈ $2,842
  - Half SE tax deductible ≈ $1,421 (adjustment to income)
  - QBI deduction (approx) = 20% × 20,100 ≈ $4,020 (subject to taxable income test)
  - These reduce your taxable income, but this is illustrative only.

4) Student loan interest
- Only interest paid in 2023 qualifies (max $2,500), and there are income phaseouts (your MAGI ~ $102k, well below MFJ thresholds for phaseout), so you should be eligible for the deduction if you actually paid interest in 2023. Provide the amount of interest you paid in 2023 (not prior years).

