- Unreimbursed employee expenses for W-2 work: not deductible currently. If related to self-employment, deduct on Schedule C instead.

6) Itemize vs. standard
- Standard deduction for MFJ in 2023 = $27,700.
- Likely conclusion: take the standard deduction unless you have substantial additional itemizable items (mortgage interest, large property taxes, much larger charitable gifts, or large medical expenses exceeding threshold). Based on your listed amounts, standard deduction is almost certainly better.

7) Forms you will likely need (Federal)
- Form 1040 (main return).
- Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments) — for adjustments such as deductible part of SE tax or student loan interest (student loan interest often on Schedule 1).
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — to report $22,100 and business expenses, including home office (or simplified method entry).
- Schedule SE — to calculate self-employment tax.
- Form 8829 — if you use the actual expense method for home office (allocate rent/utilities). Not needed if you use simplified method.
- Form 8995 (or 8995-A) — to compute QBI deduction (Form 8995 is the simpler form used if you’re under the threshold).
- Schedule B — only if total interest/dividends > $1,500.
- Form 1040-ES — if you need to make estimated tax payments for 2024 (or you had underpayment in 2023).
