1) What you can generally deduct (given your facts)
- W‑2 wages (Riverside Hospital $79,400): reported on Form 1040 (W‑2).
- Self‑employment (marketing) income $22,100: report on Schedule C. You may deduct ordinary and necessary business expenses against this income (including allowable home‑office expenses and any business supplies, advertising, etc.).
- Business interest/dividends/interest from Chase / TD Ameritrade ($920 + $290): reported as interest/dividend income (1099‑INT / 1099‑DIV) on Form 1040.
- Home office: deductible only for the self‑employment portion (not for W‑2 employment). You can use either:
  - Simplified method: $5.00 per square foot up to 300 sq ft → for 130 sq ft = $650; OR
  - Actual method: your business percentage of eligible home expenses (for rent, utilities, insurance, repairs). Your business percentage = 130 / 620 ≈ 20.97% (≈21%).
  - If you rent ($1,720/mo), the annual rent = $1,720×12 = $20,640. The business portion of rent ≈ $20,640 × 20.97% ≈ $4,330. (Other shared expenses would be prorated similarly.) Use Form 8829 if you use actual method.
- Unreimbursed expenses $1,350: only deductible if they are business expenses of your self‑employment (put on Schedule C). If these are unreimbursed employee expenses for your W‑2 job, they are NOT deductible for 2018–2025 under current law.
- Student loan interest $4,800: the student loan interest deduction is an above‑the‑line adjustment (you don’t have to itemize). The maximum deduction is $2,500 (subject to income phase‑outs). For MFJ in 2023 the phaseout begins at MAGI $145,000 and fully phases out at $175,000 — your income appears below that, so you’d be eligible for the up‑to‑$2,500 deduction (assuming the $4,800 is interest paid in 2023 on a qualified student loan and you’re otherwise eligible).
- Charitable gift $1,350 to Habitat for Humanity: deductible only if you itemize on Schedule A.

Important rule: home‑office and self‑employment business expenses reduce your Schedule C net profit and therefore reduce self‑employment tax and income tax. The student loan interest deduction and half of your self‑employment tax are adjustments to income (reduce AGI).

2) Rough numeric example (estimates for 2023)
Assumptions: all amounts you listed are amounts paid/received in 2023; the $1,350 unreimbursed expenses are business expenses for the self‑employment work. Rounded to the nearest dollar.

- Gross income:
